     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong. I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg a day**. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg a day**, and for extended-release it's **2000 mg a day**. So this dose is about twice the maximum, which raises the risk of severe GI side effects and lactic acidosis.\n\n**It may have been meant as one of these:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg a day, the IR maximum). This is a common regimen, and 1700 is exactly 2 \u00d7 850.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, split up, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **1000 mg twice daily**, or another regimen you intended.\n\nPlease tell me which one you want and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is really what you intend, I can enter it with a note recording that it's above the labeled maximum and you've confirmed it. That would usually also go to pharmacy for review."
      }
     ],
